From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar follows the display scale, as Windows' does

0814 grew the taskbar with the screen's height, as the title bars grow
(Style\Scale8): at 1080p it was 55 px, its icons and text larger than
Windows' -- "really big now on 1080p screens ... might be worth matching
the size of the bar that Windows uses. Probably a DPI issue" (David
2026-10-05). Windows sizes its taskbar by the display scale only: 40 px at
100% whatever the resolution, 60 px at 150%. The bar's scale now comes
from the display scale (LogPixels, which Settings > Display > Scale sets),
in eighths of 100%; the screen's height no longer counts.

Test: test/barscale-gate.sh with test/barscale-probe.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_BAR_NO_SCALE, SG_MUTANT_BAR_SCREEN_SCALE).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -144,10 +144,9 @@
 static HWND taskview_button;   /* Stained Glass OS: Task View, left of the desktop pager */
 static HWND pager_window;      /* Stained Glass OS: the desktop pager, left of the tray icons */
 static HWND search_button;     /* Stained Glass OS: search, beside Start */
-/* Stained Glass OS: the bar grows with the screen as the title bars do
- * (sg-shell's looks write Style\Scale8: the screen's height in eighths of
- * 800 px, 8 = as drawn here, 1080 p 11, 1200 p 12); every size of the bar
- * goes through SG_PX */
+/* Stained Glass OS: the bar is as large as the display scale makes it, as
+ * (the display's scale: LogPixels / 96, in eighths: 8 = 100%, 12 = 150%);
+ * every size of the bar goes through SG_PX */
 static int sg_s8 = 8;
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_BAR_NO_SCALE
 #define SG_PX(v) (((v) * sg_s8 + 4) / 8)
@@ -167,10 +166,20 @@
 /* the scale the looks wrote; FALSE when it is the one in use */
 static BOOL sg_load_scale(void)
 {
-    DWORD v = 8, size = sizeof(v);
+    DWORD dpi = 96, size = sizeof(dpi);
     int was = sg_s8;
-    RegGetValueW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Style", L"Scale8", RRF_RT_REG_DWORD, NULL, &v, &size );
-    sg_s8 = v < 8 ? 8 : v > 24 ? 24 : (int)v;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BAR_SCREEN_SCALE
+    /* the display's scale (Settings > Display > Scale: LogPixels), as
+     * Windows sizes its taskbar -- 40 px at 100% whatever the resolution;
+     * the screen's height made it 55 px at 1080p, larger than Windows'
+     * (David 2026-10-05) */
+    RegGetValueW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Control Panel\\Desktop", L"LogPixels", RRF_RT_REG_DWORD, NULL, &dpi, &size );
+    if (dpi < 96) dpi = 96;
+    sg_s8 = (int)min( (dpi * 8 + 48) / 96, 24 );
+#else
+    RegGetValueW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Stained Glass\\Style", L"Scale8", RRF_RT_REG_DWORD, NULL, &dpi, &size );
+    sg_s8 = dpi < 8 ? 8 : dpi > 24 ? 24 : (int)dpi;
+#endif
     return sg_s8 != was;
 }
 #define SG_SEARCH_ID 0x5345
